+---
+title: Claude Code Runtime (optional)
+sidebar_label: Claude Code Runtime
+---
+
+# Claude Code Runtime
+
+Hermes can hand `anthropic/*` turns to the [Claude Code CLI](https://docs.anthropic.com/en/docs/claude-code)
+instead of running its own tool loop. When enabled, terminal commands, file edits, permissions, hooks,
+MCP servers, skills and context compaction all happen inside Claude Code; Hermes is the shell around it:
+sessions DB, gateway platforms (Slack, Telegram, Discord, ...), slash commands and memory.
+
+This is the Anthropic-side twin of the [Codex App-Server Runtime](./codex-app-server-runtime.md).
+It is **opt-in only**; default behaviour is unchanged.
+
+## Why
+
+- Run Claude turns against your **Claude subscription** with the same auth Claude Code uses (`claude /login`),
+  or an API key / proxy passed through explicitly.
+- Use **Claude Code's own toolset**: `Bash`, `Read`, `Edit`, `Write`, `Grep`, `Glob`, `WebFetch`, subagents,
+  plus every MCP server, hook, skill and plugin configured in `~/.claude`.
+- A gateway session becomes **one Claude Code session**: the same transcript on disk, resumed across
+  Hermes restarts, so a Slack thread is literally a colleague's Claude Code session.
+
+## Enable
+
+```yaml
+model:
+  provider: anthropic             # any provider works; the CLI brings its own auth
+  default: claude-opus-5          # passed as --model when it is a Claude id or alias
+  anthropic_runtime: claude_code  # the switch
+  claude_code:                    # all optional
+    binary: claude
+    permission_mode: acceptEdits  # default | acceptEdits | plan | bypassPermissions
+    allowed_tools: []             # --allowedTools, e.g. ["Bash", "Read", "Edit"]
+    extra_args: []                # anything else for `claude -p`
+    env_passthrough: []           # e.g. ["ANTHROPIC_API_KEY", "ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL"]
+    turn_timeout_seconds: 1800
+```
+
+`bypassPermissions` maps to `--dangerously-skip-permissions`; it is also chosen automatically when an
+approval bypass is active (`approvals.mode: off`, `--yolo`, `HERMES_YOLO_MODE`). Otherwise `-p` mode has no
+one to answer permission prompts, so anything outside the mode's allowance is refused by Claude Code.
+
+The child inherits a login-shell environment only (`HOME`, `PATH`, locale, XDG, `CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR`, certs);
+provider keys the Hermes process uses are **not** inherited unless listed in `env_passthrough`.
+
+## How it works
+
+- One `claude -p --input-format stream-json --output-format stream-json --verbose` process per agent,
+  reused across turns; `--session-id` on the first turn, `--resume` when the transcript already exists
+  (the id is derived from the Hermes session id).
+- `assistant` / `user` (tool_result) events are projected into Hermes' message shape and flushed to the
+  session DB; tool_use / tool_result pairs drive the gateway's tool-progress and task-card callbacks.
+- The `result` event ends the turn: its `result` text is the reply, its `usage` and `total_cost_usd` feed
+  Hermes accounting.
+- Interrupts send the stream-json `control_request` interrupt frame. Steering is queued for the next turn.
+- Hermes context compression is a no-op on this runtime: Claude Code compacts its own transcript.
+
+## Not covered
+
+- Codex-style approval callbacks (Claude Code decides from its permission mode and settings).
+- Streaming text deltas (Claude Code emits whole assistant messages; the gateway posts the final reply).
